# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANJOY888 multi-camera custom firmware workspace -- git ignore rules
#
# Layout:
#   stock/<CAM>/   pristine vendor .bin images      -> TRACKED (already xz-compressed)
#   builds/<CAM>/  editable rootfs + header.bin    -> TRACKED (this is where edits live)
#   out/           packed flashable images          -> IGNORED (reproducible via pack.sh)
#   tools/         unpack/repack + helpers          -> TRACKED
#
# Philosophy: track SOURCE (rootfs trees, headers, scripts, docs).
# Ignore everything reproducible (packed .bin, squashfs) and all secret material.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Packed firmware images: reproducible via ./pack.sh --------------------
# Everything we build lands in out/ and is never committed.
out/

# --- Generated squashfs (reproducible via mksquashfs / pack.sh) -----------
*.squashfs

# --- Extracted scratch artifacts (regenerated by extract.sh) --------------
# header.bin and build.info under builds/ ARE tracked (needed for repack +
# block-size detection); any stray copies elsewhere are not.
/tail.bin
/rootfs.squashfs

# --- Private TLS key material (NEVER commit) ------------------------------
# Generated at repack time by pack.sh; each build gets its own cert.
*.key
*.pwd
*.pem
https.key
https.pwd
https.crt
builds/**/opt/ch/https.key
builds/**/opt/ch/https.pwd
builds/**/opt/ch/https.crt

# --- Recovery telnet password (generated by pack.sh, NEVER commit) --------
reclogin.pass
builds/**/opt/ch/reclogin.pass
tools/.reclogin.pass
tools/.reclogin_pass

# --- Editor / OS cruft ---------------------------------------------------
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Local scratch -------------------------------------------------------
/tmp/
*.log

# --- Nagios shim build intermediates -------------------------------------
# The compiled shim that ships is builds/<cam>/rootfs/opt/ch/nagios_authd.so
# (tracked, because pack.sh reads the rootfs tree directly). Everything else
# under tools/nagios_shim/ that is a compiled binary is reproducible from the
# .c sources via build_shim.sh, so it is not committed.
tools/nagios_shim/*.so
tools/nagios_shim/authprobe_dyn
tools/nagios_shim/authprobe_static
tools/.reclogin_pass.*

# --- Local camera addresses (NEVER commit) ---------------------------------
# Real LAN addresses live only here. tools/cam (and everything that calls it)
# resolves hosts from this file; tools/cameras.conf.example is the tracked
# template and uses RFC5737 TEST-NET addresses.
# Note: this pattern does NOT match cameras.conf.example (gitignore matches
# whole path components, not string prefixes), so the template stays tracked.
tools/cameras.conf

# PII gate's private needle list (real IPs/MACs/passwords). Never commit.
tools/.pii_needles
